WARNING
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The user data are saved within the DyboApp Resources folder, upgrading
to a newer version may result in the lost of user data.

Before installing a newer DyboApp version, the user should make a
backup of its Resources folder.

When installing a newer version of the DyboApp (from a ZIP archive),
the user should request a merging installation, this operation depends
on the Archive software used to install the DyboApp.


HOW TO START
----------------------------------------------------------------------
When the DyboApp is installed in the user disk space, double click on
the file "start.sh".  Check the start.sh file has the execution flag
set.

When the the DyboApp is installed in a read-only folder, run the
application with its "startMultiUser.sh" script; adjust its USERDATA
variable to indicate the location in the user disk space to save data,
by default it is set to "$HOME/Documents/myDybo".
